, routine Falcon 9 cadence.\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Bull Case\",[[0,9,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"$300B – $350B+\",[[0,14,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Operational Starship deploying V3/V4 Starlink, Direct-to-Cell mass commercial rollout, spin-off speculation.\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,[null,0,\"Note: As SpaceX remains a private entity, these figures reflect secondary share sales, tender offers, and consensus estimates from institutional space-economy analysts (e.g., Morgan Stanley, Ark Invest).\",[[0,203,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Key Upside Catalysts\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Starlink Free Cash Flow Expansion\",[[0,33,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Starlink accounts for the lion’s share of enterprise value expansion. Increasing enterprise, maritime, and aviation broadband contracts, combined with high-margin Direct-to-Cell partnerships with global telecom operators, accelerate top-line recurring revenue.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Starship Operational Milestones\",[[0,31,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Transitioning Starship from test flights to routine orbital payload delivery radically drops the cost per kilogram to orbit. Successfully using Starship to deploy full-size next-gen Starlink satellites multiplies network capacity and lowers launch costs compared to Falcon 9.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Defense and Government Contracts\",[[0,32,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Expanded awards under the U.S. Space Force National Security Space Launch (NSSL) Phase 3, along with dedicated Starshield deployments and continued Artemis Human Landing System (HLS) milestones, secure multibillion-dollar backlogs with guaranteed margins.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Starlink IPO / Partial Spin-Off Talk\",[[0,36,[[null,null,nul