n Starlink satellites multiplies network capacity and lowers launch costs compared to Falcon 9.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Defense and Government Contracts\",[[0,32,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Expanded awards under the U.S. Space Force National Security Space Launch (NSSL) Phase 3, along with dedicated Starshield deployments and continued Artemis Human Landing System (HLS) milestones, secure multibillion-dollar backlogs with guaranteed margins.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Starlink IPO / Partial Spin-Off Talk\",[[0,36,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Any firm institutional step or SEC filing toward spinning out Starlink into a separate publicly traded company typically triggers a multiple re-rating on SpaceX’s holding valuation.\"]]]]],1]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Key Downside Risks\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Starship Development \\u0026 Reliability Bottlenecks\",[[0,46,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Any major setbacks in rapid reusability or in-orbit refueling could delay Artemis moon missions and bottleneck the deployment of higher-throughput Starlink constellations, prolonging expensive R\\u0026D cash burn.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Regulatory \\u0026 Environmental Friction\",[[0,35,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Stringent FAA launch licensing reviews, environmental challenges regarding the Starbase (Boca Chica) or\"]]]]],1]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1002,\"Don't personalize\",2,null,[\"person_cancel\",\"https://fo